{"title":"2003 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 15","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><dl><dd><i>The following problem is from the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_12A_Problems\" title=\"2003 AMC 12A Problems\">2003 AMC 12A #15</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_10A_Problems\" title=\"2003 AMC 10A Problems\">2003 AMC 10A #19</a>, so those problems redirect to this page.</i></dd></dl>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_SpreadTheMathLove\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by SpreadTheMathLove</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Semicircle\" title=\"Semicircle\">semicircle</a> of <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Diameter\" title=\"Diameter\">diameter</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> sits at the top of a semicircle of diameter <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, as shown. The shaded <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Area\" title=\"Area\">area</a> inside the smaller semicircle and outside the larger semicircle is called a <i>lune</i>. Determine the area of this lune. \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/8/ee832dfa1925af1fe40d6af62243894f0614e222.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] import graph; size(150); defaultpen(fontsize(8)); pair A=(-2,0), B=(2,0); filldraw(Arc((0,sqrt(3)),1,0,180)--cycle,mediumgray); filldraw(Arc((0,0),2,0,180)--cycle,white); draw(2*expi(2*pi/6)--2*expi(4*pi/6));  label(&quot;1&quot;,(0,sqrt(3)),(0,-1)); label(&quot;2&quot;,(0,0),(0,-1)); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"185\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/e/5ae901a30a3a90c0797cce16c631c5fda5d78d5a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(A) \\ } \\frac{1}{6}\\pi-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4}\\qquad \\mathrm{(B) \\ } \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4}-\\frac{1}{12}\\pi\\qquad \\mathrm{(C) \\ } \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4}-\\frac{1}{24}\\pi\\qquad \\mathrm{(D) \\ } \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4}+\\frac{1}{24}\\pi\\qquad \\mathrm{(E) \\ } \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4}+\\frac{1}{12}\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"705\" height=\"41\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7dc6582f0dd4a6d448e272a4a65408d00646000.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] import graph; size(150); defaultpen(fontsize(8)); pair A=(-2,0), B=(2,0); filldraw(Arc((0,sqrt(3)),1,0,180)--cycle,mediumgray); fill(Arc((0,0),2,0,180)--cycle,white); draw(Arc((0,0),2,0,180)--cycle); draw((0,0)--2*expi(2*pi/6)--2*expi(2*pi/6*2)--(0,0));  label(&quot;A&quot;,(0,2),(0,4)); label(&quot;B&quot;,(0,2),(0,-1)); label(&quot;C&quot;,(0,sqrt(3)/2),(0,2)); label(&quot;1&quot;,(-0.5,sqrt(3)/2),(-1,0)); label(&quot;1&quot;,(0.5,sqrt(3)/2),(1,0)); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"172\" />\n</p><p><br />\nThe shaded area <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/7/5974998abb6495b7e7cb9c32143687050121fe86.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[A]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" /> is equal to the area of the smaller semicircle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/1/ae1d8ff00ee5641906bcafa9a9ec1e98cb41498a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[A+B]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"62\" height=\"20\" /> minus the area of a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Sector\" title=\"Sector\">sector</a> of the larger circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/7/d77dc2c402c80073c4eb779f64c4b3c5fbc1d9c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[B+C]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"59\" height=\"18\" /> plus the area of a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Triangle\" title=\"Triangle\">triangle</a> formed by two <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Radius\" title=\"Radius\"> radii</a> of the larger semicircle and the diameter of the smaller semicircle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/b/8eb0d5cccb9df6a659750553ad358f3f7c446956.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[C]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"22\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>The area of the smaller semicircle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/1/2b1643c5c18b6fa64bbd187553753154798d61c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[A+B] = \\frac{1}{2}\\pi\\cdot\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)^{2}=\\frac{1}{8}\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"216\" height=\"46\" />. \n</p><p>Since the radius of the larger semicircle is equal to the diameter of the smaller half circle, the triangle is an equilateral triangle and the sector measures <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/f/29fa0a9949f018e121b2093216dd5db13d3abef0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"28\" height=\"15\" />. \n</p><p>The area of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/f/29fa0a9949f018e121b2093216dd5db13d3abef0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"28\" height=\"15\" /> sector of the larger semicircle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/8/bc879f9abc0c3162da87a9924837e849fe35b677.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[B+C] = \\frac{60}{360}\\pi\\cdot\\left(\\frac{2}{2}\\right)^{2}=\\frac{1}{6}\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"235\" height=\"46\" />. \n</p><p>The area of the triangle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/3/1e3b9d2aae4c54ac73fe5f02af335976a89ee9db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[C] = \\frac{1^{2}\\sqrt{3}}{4}=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"144\" height=\"41\" />.\n</p><p>So the shaded area is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/1/851075ddcae6c08caa75052db7fd1cbfec7b9ca9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[A] = [A+B]-[B+C]+[C] = \\left(\\frac{1}{8}\\pi\\right)-\\left(\\frac{1}{6}\\pi\\right)+\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4}\\right)=\\boxed{\\mathrm{(C)}\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4}-\\frac{1}{24}\\pi}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"616\" height=\"57\" />. We have thus solved the problem.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_SpreadTheMathLove\">Video Solution by SpreadTheMathLove</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by SpreadTheMathLove\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-4qnOdE0Dyk\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-4qnOdE0Dyk</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_10A\" title=\"2003 AMC 10A\">2003 AMC 10A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_10A_Problems\" title=\"2003 AMC 10A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_10A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2003 AMC 10A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2003 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 18\">Problem 18</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2003 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 20\">Problem 20</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_1\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2003 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_2\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2003 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> 